Z||000003||Wolfhound||04-13-2001||10:17 AM||||Chadman , the engines a big block Caddy to.<BR>Mark Collins builds racing engines for some of the guy he races. Oh, The Toyota Land Crusier in the background has a 327 Chevy installed "Scarry". Jim Devier builds Houses. (DevierBuilt Fine Homes).<P>Huntsville speedway is billed as the fastest 1/2 mile in the country. Extremly high banked corners.<P>here is a link: <A HREF="http://www.huntsvillespeedway.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.huntsvillespeedway.com</A><P>I just checked the link, It starts with a before and after shot of a wreck at mobile speedway. Wow!<P>Mark races again tonight and you can get race result on site, if you're intrested. I,m going to try to make it up before the race. I,m starting a job there tommorrow.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||04-13-2001||11:01 AM||||What a cool track!  Now that's roots racing.  Wouldn't it be cool to drag Dario Franchitti and Ashley Judd to Huntsville Speedway and force them to eat hot dogs and watch Mini Stocks?<P>I still think it would be great fun to watch 20 guys in basically-stock 84 4-sp Fieros go fender-banging around a bullring like that for 50 laps or so.  It would be way more fun to BE one of the 20 guys...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||04-14-2001||12:51 AM||||A guy that came over to give us an estimate on some work (saw all my Fieros) was telling my wife about a track where he races, somewhere in Alabama.<BR>Supposedly, the <I>only</I> rule is that you have to be driving an American car. No imports. Everything runs at the same time.<BR>He said that whenever someone brings out a Fiero that it just <I>cleans house</I>.<BR>Last I heard, they were trying to decide if they were going to create a different class, because the competition was so "stacked" in favor of the Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||04-19-2001||06:28 AM||||I made it to Huntsville about 20 minutes before the race Friday. It didn't go to well for Mark, He started 7th and had made it to 4th when the lug nuts pulled through the right front wheel.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fttlmlw.JPG">  <BR>As Kenny rogers says "You picked a fine time to leave me loose wheel"<P>Raydar, I overheard some talk about the track you mentioned while we were at the races. supposedly some guy started to build a lake and decided to turn it into a round track. It,s dirt from what I understand. They run match races and only a few cars at a time.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||04-19-2001||09:16 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>As Kenny rogers says "You picked a fine time to leave me loose wheel"<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I hate it when that happens.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Must be some incredible G-loads on those cars for that to happen, though.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
